//==============================================================================
// uart_alert_tx.v   (GENERATED by gen_uart.py - the text ROM and token table are
//                    produced by script so string lengths/addresses cannot drift)
//
// Alert record formatter + CRC-16 + UART transmitter, all in the 100 MHz domain.
//
//   clk_a domain (alert_collector)  --[325-bit record, toggle req/ack]-->  here
//
// Each alert is sent as ONE line of JSON-like text, e.g.
//
// {"v":1,"t":1,"id":123,"up":125034,"sev":"HIGH","rule":"TCP_SYN_FLOOD","rid":1,
//  "smac":"02:11:22:33:44:55","dmac":"AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF","sip":"192.168.1.20",
//  "dip":"192.168.1.10","pr":"TCP","sp":49152,"dp":80,"ev":"SYN_PER_WINDOW",
//  "val":214,"st":"THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED","sup":0,"lost":0,"crc":"9A3F"}\r\n
//
// (one physical line, wrapped above).  Each line is one valid JSON object: all
// strings are fixed ASCII identifiers, so nothing ever needs escaping.
//
//   v    protocol version (1)            t    message type: 1 = alert, 2 = heartbeat
//   id   alert sequence number           up   uptime in ms when the event happened
//   sev  INFO/LOW/HIGH/CRITICAL          rule/rid  detection rule name / numeric id
//   smac/dmac/sip/dip  endpoints         pr/sp/dp  L4 protocol, source/dest port
//   ev   name of the evidence metric     val  its value (count, length, port ...)
//   st   rule status                     sup  same-rule events suppressed (rate limit)
//   lost alerts dropped by full queues   crc  CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE (poly 0x1021,
//                                        init 0xFFFF, no reflection, no xor-out)
//                                        over every byte from '{' up to and
//                                        including the '"' that opens the crc value.
//
// Heartbeat (t = 2) every HEARTBEAT_MS:
//   {"v":1,"t":2,"id":5,"up":125034,"st":"ALIVE","crc":"1A2B"}\r\n
//
// Record layout received on x_data (must match alert_collector.v):
//   [324:317] rid  [316:309] ev  [308:306] st  [305:304] sev  [303:280] id
//   [279:248] up   [247:200] smac [199:152] dmac [151:120] sip [119:88] dip
//   [87:80] proto  [79:64] sport [63:48] dport  [47:32] val  [31:16] sup [15:0] lost
//
// Clock-domain crossing: x_req is a toggle from clk_a; it is double-registered
// here.  x_data is held stable by the sender until x_ack (also a toggle) comes
// back, so the wide bus is sampled only while quiescent.
//==============================================================================
